On Thursday evening at half past five, I arrive at the club.
I rent a racket from reception as always.
Then I go towards my court.
Neha is already waiting for me there.
She laughs upon seeing me and says, "Are you ready to lose today, Maya?"
I also smile and reply, "Dreaming is a good thing, Neha!"
We warm up and the game begins.
Today's match is very tough.
We both try our best for every point.
Neha hits the shuttlecock very fast.
I run and send it back.
"You are running very fast!" Neha says jokingly.
"I have to run to beat you," I say while taking a deep breath.
The score is running absolutely even.
In the end, I play a good shot and win the point.
"Wow, that was an amazing shot!" Neha says clapping.
I really like playing badminton with Neha.
Today's match against Neha is very exciting.
Next Thursday's match gets fixed too.
